{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Accuracy validation added five implementation-backed corrections.\n\n- Jira project configuration is required by src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/access_check.py, runtime.py, and src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py. docs/config.md, docs/jira-sync-setup.md, bridge-probe help, and generated CLI help still describe a DIG fallback or call JIRA_PROJECT optional.\n- docs/identity-setup.md rejects GITHUB_ENV as an unreliable cross-step channel. Four maintained workflows use GITHUB_ENV for REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY, and additional workflows use it for other later-step values.\n- docs/README.md still describes six ticket relations and files completed plans, handoffs, migration records, and validation transcripts as repository documentation. The current model has seven relations. The supplied taxonomy assigns work history to tickets and reserves internal documentation for current state.\n- pyproject.toml includes only LICENSE in license-files. The bundled alias wordlist cites docs/licenses/adjective-adjective-animal-LICENSE.txt, so distribution metadata and NOTICE need a complete third-party provenance and packaging review.\n- ADR 0042 and ADR 0090 declare Accepted after an explicit supersession notice. scripts/check_adr_numbers.py validates numbering, markers, and links but does not validate lifecycle metadata or relationship consistency.\n\nNo project files changed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787289724930354001,"uuid":"f51ad97a-c553-4efd-aa4a-f5a36715b0af"}